      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-8157",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075254/assets/c3a4052f80fc4a7202d410f3ea523e58507ac60399506c2abad9be164bce5251.png)\nConsider the matrix $P$ shown above. Given that $A=PDP^T$ is an orthogonal diagonalization of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ for some diagonal matrix $D,$ which of the following could be the first column of the matrix $P?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14075254/assets/18abb9c5165a3fe54a0f3067cf5325bfd4bd0fa4243c841ce4e7bb95c25dddda.png)",
